From 6b634c3c7770d0d5f6a3c886be1e5c611533174c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:30:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/19] token-prefix cache: reuse conversation prefix tokens
 per request [w6-6 a4-s1]

Stateless clients (pi) resend the whole conversation every round; the server
re-tokenized all of it (75 ms @131k tokens) even when 99% of the tokens were
identical to the previous request.

server_token_prefix_cache (server-common) keeps the last prompts per
(add_special, parse_special) with their token streams and byte spans. On a
prefix hit the token stream is spliced: cached prefix + freshly tokenized
tail, where the splice point is always the start of a special-token fragment
(a hard boundary of tokenizer_st_partition; BPE fragments tokenize
independently, so the result is bit-identical to a full tokenization).

Safety rails: BPE vocabularies only (SPM/WPM/UGM keep cross-fragment state
and are bypassed); every entry is verified at creation (token pieces must
re-spell the prompt exactly, else the vocab is not cached); the first splices
are self-checked against a full tokenization and any mismatch disables the
cache; LLAMA_SERVER_TOKEN_PREFIX_CACHE=0 disables it outright.

Wired into handle_completions_impl only (chat/completions hot path); token
stream is unchanged for the prompt cache / park downstream (same key: the
produced tokens are identical by gate).

tests/test-token-prefix-cache.cpp: bit-identity gate over a synthetic
multilingual corpus (CJK, thinking blocks, tool-call JSON, adjacent/partial
special markers), growing conversations, mid-prefix edits, full hits, flag
changes, concurrency; bypass assertions for SPM. With the real pi prompt
(412 KB / 131k tokens): 16/16 rounds bit-identical, tokenize 618 -> 114 ms
over the round series (5.4x); e2e template+tokenize @873 KB warm 4.8x.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai
